message:
use lambda-sort, drop old custom code

 the lambda sort function requires -std=c++0x or -std=gnu++0x,
           // first supported in gnu 4.5, but our usage here busts in 4.5.2
           // and may first work in 4.6, not yet available pre-packaged for
           // Ubuntu 11.04.

requires c++0x and later and gcc 4.5+ which is now ok

testutils: use return False immediately

return right away, instead of carrying a result=false value all over,
this is helpful to see what part of the check method errored.

