Removed empty "constraints" parameters from specs #2369

SWIG error translating size_t to unsigned int creating redefinition to the latter type

Known problem and solution: See nupic/py/bindings/algorithms/algorithms_impl.i   around line 1000
// Already seen by swig on linux32 where size_t is the same size as unsigned int
%template(Size_T_Vector) std::vector<size_t>;

The error comes from a different point. Suggestion is to wrap in the nupic/lang/common/engine_internal_common.i  the

%template(Dimset) std::vector<size_t>;

in an #ifndef

//32bit fix
%template(Dimset) std::vector<size_t>;

encoders keep topology of input data

for 1D vectors everything stays the same,
newly supports 2D (3D ,...) arrays in encoder.encode()

testutils: use return False immediately

return right away, instead of carrying a result=false value all over,
this is helpful to see what part of the check method errored.

Multi: use default array transfor as list

because list keeps data-types [3, 'hi', 4];
while numpy.array() -> numpy.ndarray converts all to string if one is present

