Scripting improvements

Now possible to classify objects by intensity using a QP static method;
also improved default colors within PathClassFactory

Improve macro parallelisation, handling cells

This now always passes an overlay if a Roi is required, which makes it possible to include nuclei along with cell ROIs.

Here's an example macro showing how a mean intensity measurement can be made inside a cell and then inside the nucleus (assuming the nucleus is available). It works by activating the 'next' Roi in the overlay; when we have cells, the selected object should always be first in the overlay, and the main cell boundary should also always be before the nucleus.
```groovy
name = replace(Property.getSliceLabel, " ", "_");

getStatistics(area, mean);
Roi.setProperty("qupath.object.measurements.ImageJ_cell_" + name, mean);

Overlay.activateSelection(1);
getStatistics(area, mean);
Roi.setProperty("qupath.object.measurements.ImageJ_nucleus_" + name, mean);
```

This commit also switches how macros are run in parallel. The method here seems more robust when running many small tasks in different threads.

Fix exception when removing large numbers of measurements in a script

Fixes https://github.com/qupath/qupath/issues/915
Using an array is enough to overcome the problem.

The following script helps quickly add many measurements to a selected object:
```
def pathObject = getSelectedObject()
def measurements = []
try (def ml = pathObject.getMeasurementList()) {
    for (int i = 0; i < 500; i++) {
        def n = "Measurement $i"
        measurements << n
        ml.putMeasurement(n, i*2)
    }
}
```

Initial color deconvolution support

This hard-codes stains for each channel when the script is generated.

A workaround for a script is to to use something like this:
```
def myStains = getCurrentImageData().getColorDeconvolutionStains()
qupath.imagej.gui.scripts.ImageJScriptRunner.fromMap(text: """
getStatistics(area, mean);
Roi.setProperty("qupath.object.measurements.ImageJ_mean_" + Property.getSliceLabel, mean);
""", channels: [[stains: myStains, stainNumber: 2]], ...)
```
